<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Tough trading conditions knock Foschini.</title>
<headline>Tough trading conditions knock Foschini.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-11-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year ended September 28</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr, attrib (cts)     35.9	  vs 41.9</p>
<p>    Attrib income	   74.6	  vs 87.0</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   111.4	 vs 133.7</p>
<p>    Tax			 36.8	  vs 46.7</p>
<p>    Interest paid	   29.3	  vs 25.2</p>
<p>Full name: Foschini Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - Retailer Foschini gave no turnover breakdown but said turnover in the half year increased by 6.1 percent over the year-ago period.</p>
<p>The company said difficult trading conditions had been caused in large measure by high levels of consumer indebtedness created by a proliferation of credit offerings, as well as a fiercely competitive market.</p>
<p>It said it was too early to be definitive on trading prospects for the full year.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
